"comparison": "Both Citigroup (C) and Bank of America (BAC) disclose the election of the fair value option for specific debt instruments. C reports that short-term borrowings and long-term debt are accounted for at amortized cost, except where the Company has elected to report debt instruments (including certain structured notes) at fair value. Similarly, BAC elects to account for certain short-term borrowings, primarily short-term structured liabilities, under the fair value option because this debt is risk-managed on a fair value basis. While C's disclosure focuses on the general accounting policy exception for structured notes, BAC specifies the operational rationale (risk management) for similar structured liability electives.",
