"comparison": "Both companies address the accounting mechanics for debt instruments where fair value changes or adjustments impact the carrying value and subsequent interest expense. C states that changes in fair value of debt instruments carried at fair value are recorded in Principal transactions, with credit adjustments in OCI, and that premiums/discounts for amortized cost debt are amortized using the effective interest method. BAC discloses that fair value adjustments from de-designated hedges on long-term debt decreased carrying values and that these adjustments are amortized or accreted into interest over the contractual lives. Both disclosures illustrate the interaction between fair value adjustments/hedging and the amortization or interest expense recognition over the life of the debt.",
